Source: ai-switch
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Maintainer: ai-switch packagers <ai-switch@localhost>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), dh-python, python3
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: ai-switch
Architecture: all
Depends: ${python3:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, python3 (>= 3.9)
Description: explicitly turn system-level AI features on or off
 ai-switch finds the AI features built into a Linux system (browser AI
 policies, vendor assistants, local LLM services) and lets you turn each one
 off or on with one explicit command. Every change is journaled with the state
 before it, so "ai-switch revert" puts the system back exactly as it was.
 Nothing changes without a command; packages are removed only with --purge.
 .
 An apt hook re-applies your choices after updates. It only acts when
 ai-switch has changed something on the machine.

Package: ai-switch-gui
Architecture: all
Depends: ai-switch (= ${binary:Version}), ${python3:Depends}, ${misc:Depends},
 python3-gi, gir1.2-gtk-4.0, gir1.2-adw-1, pkexec
Description: window for ai-switch, with a polkit-guarded helper
 A GTK 4 / libadwaita window with one switch per AI feature. It runs without
 privileges and changes things through pkexec and
 /usr/libexec/ai-switch-helper, which accepts module ids only (no --purge,
 --root or --all).
